// "Has Solid Bodies", authored in Blockly — impenetrability, in blocks.
//
// The engine's version was a single step with the whole of AABB resolution
// inside it. This is the same behaviour decomposed into members, because the
// step is the readable part once the arithmetic has names: for each mover, for
// each solid, push it out. Everything else is a block with a name — `collision
// size of`, `is touching`, `push … out of … over …`.
//
// It keeps the two traits separate for the same reason the engine did: a Solid
// body blocks every side, while gravity's "Acts as Ground" is a surface you may
// pass up through. A tile carries both; they were never the same thing.
//
// Stored as the workspace JSON a `.rule` file holds, because that IS the format:
// importing it copies these bytes into `rules/solid.rule` and the learner
// opens the same workspace this was written in.

